{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1001", "sample_idx": 43, "model_name": "mistralai/mistral-small-4-119b-2603", "content": "**A Most Wondrous Journey to the Land of the Rising Sun**\n\n**Act I: Scene I – The Arrival in the Realm of the Rising Sun**\n\nUpon the morrow’s morn when golden Phoebus doth ascend the heavens thee shalt set foot in the famed isle of Nippon. Alight from thy vessel at the grand port of Yokohama where the spirits of modernity and tradition do dance in merry accord. Take swift repose in a ryokan of old where tatami mats and futons shall cradle thee in slumber most divine.\n\n**Act I: Scene II – The Ancient Capital of Nara**\n\nUpon the third day ride forth to Nara the cradle of Japan’s past. Behold the colossal Buddha at Tōdai-ji its gaze both stern and serene as though it doth guard the very soul of the land. Wander through the sacred groves where stags do roam as lords of the realm untamed. Pray at the Kasuga Taisha whose lanterns glimmer like stars snatched from the firmament.\n\n**Act II: Scene I – The Imperial Splendor of Kyoto**\n\nWith haste make thy way to Kyoto the imperial city where the ghosts of emperors do linger in every stone and stream. Spend four days in reverence and marvel:\n\n**Day One:** At the Kinkaku-ji the Golden Pavilion its topmost spire gleaming like a jewel plucked from the crown of a sun god.\n\n**Day Two:** At the Arashiyama Bamboo Grove where emerald shafts ascend to heaven and the wind doth weave a melody most sweet.\n\n**Day Three:** At the Fushimi Inari Shrine where torii gates form a crimson river winding up the sacred mountain. Climb to the summit if thy spirit is bold and be rewarded with a vista that shall steal thy breath away.\n\n**Day Four:** In the Gion district where geisha and maiko do glide like specters of elegance. Should fortune favor thee thou mayst spy one in passing and catch a glimpse of a world untouched by time.\n\n**Act III: Scene I – The Floating World of Osaka**\n\nDepart Kyoto and venture to Osaka the kitchen of Japan where the air doth carry the scent of takoyaki and okonomiyaki. Spend two days in mirth and gluttony:\n\n**Day One:** At the Dotonbori where neon signs do blaze like the fires of a thousand suns and the river doth reflect their gaudy glory.\n\n**Day Two:** At the Osaka Castle its mighty walls and golden adornments a testament to the power of princes of old. Climb to the top and gaze upon the city that doth surge and thrive beneath thee.\n\n**Act IV: Scene I – The Modern Marvel of Tokyo**\n\nNow to Tokyo do make thy final pilgrimage a city of wonders both gleaming and bewildering. Spend four days in its embrace:\n\n**Day One:** At the Shibuya Crossing where humanity doth flow like a river in spate and the billboards do shout their messages in hues most garish.\n\n**Day Two:** At the Senso-ji Temple in Asakusa where the Thunder Gate doth mark the path to enlightenment. Seek thy fortune in the omikuji and wander the Nakamise-dori where wares most curious and sweet are sold.\n\n**Day Three:** At the teamLab Planets where digital art doth surround thee and transform thee into a being of another world.\n\n**Day Four:** At the Meiji Shrine where the forest doth enfold thee in its verdant embrace and the torii gates do mark the path to the spirit of the emperor.\n\n**Epilogue: Scene I – The Farewell**\n\nOn the fifteenth day when the moon doth wax full thee shalt depart from the land of the Rising Sun with memories most precious in thy heart. Yet fear not for the spirits of Japan shall linger in thy soul and call thee back to its shores anew. Thus endeth thy journey in this most wondrous of lands.", "logprobs": [{"token": "**", "logprob": -0.5259684324264526}, {"token": "A", "logprob": -0.03410419076681137}, {"token": " Most", "logprob": -0.7773334980010986}, {"token": " W", "logprob": -0.4359798729419708}, {"token": "ond", "logprob": -1.2993727978027891e-05}, {"token": "rous", "logprob": -5.006777428206988e-06}, {"token": " Journey", "logpr